ated it so by  the time I was in college I was really a  closeted Christian because in college at  least at that time it wasn't very cool  to be spiritual it wasn't cool to go to  church  so I hid it I buried it really deep I  went to NYU I got an acting degree in  1989 I graduated and then I went to Los  Angeles to pursue acting and I knew  pretty much from the very beginning of  trying to pursue acting that I was not  going to succeed because it was all  about put yourself out there and sell  yourself and things that are just  completely not me  so just took a job in advertising to pay  the bills and that job led to a 20-year  career and motion picture advertising I  worked on print campaigns for all the  big movies a lot of my work ended up on  posters for The Hobbit franchise the  Batman franchise The Expendables that  was a really complicated shoot the  people in that job we're making 100  hundred fifty thousand dollars a year  but every time I would drive past the  church every time I would hear something  about God I would think that's where I'm  supposed to be and I think like most  people I felt like I wanted something  more out of my life I wanted something  deeper and more meaningful I didn't feel  like I was doing something meaningful I  felt like I was doing something just to  make money it wasn't until the late 90s  I had been dating a guy for about five  years but he was an atheist and he knew  that I was Christian he knew as a  believer but I really suppressed that I  really pushed it down and he and I got  married and we went on our honeymoon  to Paris and I remember I walked into  Notre Dom with my brand-new husband and  I completely burst into tears because I  was so overwhelmed by the presence of  God if I hadn't been so self-conscious I  would have fallen down on my knees in  the middle of the church and sobbed but  I just stood there crying and my atheist  husband said to me what's going on Mike  what's happening and I thought I still  want to 